#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1
msgid "Package Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:3
msgid ""
"moon uses a package file to identify and describe a package. The legacy "
"format is `moon.pkg.json`, and the new format is `moon.pkg`. For full "
"JSON schema, please check [moon's "
"repository](https://github.com/moonbitlang/moon/blob/main/crates/moonbuild/template/pkg.schema.json)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:7
msgid ""
"`moon.pkg.json` is no longer accepted by ordinary toolchain commands. Use "
"`moon fmt` to migrate existing JSON manifests before checking or building. "
"The JSON examples below are migration references, not configurations for new"
" projects."
msgstr ""
"通常のツールチェーンコマンドは `moon.pkg.json` を受け付けなくなりました。チェックやビルドの前に `moon fmt` で既存の "
"JSON 設定ファイルを移行してください。以下の JSON の例は移行用の参考であり、新しいプロジェクト向けの設定ではありません。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:12
msgid "New format (`moon.pkg`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:14
msgid ""
"The new format is a concise DSL. You can generate or reformat it from an "
"existing `moon.pkg.json` with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:17
msgid "moon -C <module_dir> fmt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:21
#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:321
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:23
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"moonbit-community/language/packages/virtual\",\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")\n"
"\n"
"options(\n"
"  overrides: [ \"moonbit-community/language/packages/implement\" ],\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:27
msgid ""
"In `moon.pkg`, dependencies are declared in an `import { ... }` block. "
"Use `@alias` to set a custom alias:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:30
#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:199
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgA\",\n"
"  \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgC\" @c,\n"
"  \"moonbitlang/core/builtin\",\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:34
msgid ""
"Simple package settings can be written directly, using underscore-separated "
"names, for example `proof_enabled = true` or `regex_backend = \"table\"`. "
"Declarations such as `formatter`, `pkgtype`, and `virtual` have dedicated "
"top-level forms. `moon fmt` migrates supported settings from `options(...)` "
"to these forms. Legacy keys that remain inside `options` and contain `-` "
"must be quoted."
msgstr ""
"単純なパッケージ設定は、`proof_enabled = true` や `regex_backend = \"table\"` "
"のように、アンダースコア区切りの名前で直接記述できます。`formatter`、`pkgtype`、`virtual` "
"などには専用のトップレベル宣言があります。`moon fmt` は対応する設定を `options(...)` "
"からこれらの形式に移行します。`options` に残る従来のキーで `-` を含むものは引用符で囲む必要があります。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:41 ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:1257
msgid "virtual(has_default: true)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:45
msgid "The `moon.pkg` format allows comments `//...`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:47
msgid "Full syntax of `moon.pkg` is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:49
msgid ""
"moon_pkg ::= statement*\n"
"statement ::= import | assign | apply\n"
"\n"
"import ::= \"import\" \"{\" (import_item \",\")* import_item? \"}\" "
"import_kind?\n"
"import_item ::= STRING (\"@\" PKG_NAME)?\n"
"import_kind ::= \"for\" STRING\n"
"\n"
"assign ::= LIDENT \"=\" expr\n"
"\n"
"apply ::= LIDENT \"(\" (argument \",\")* argument? \")\"\n"
"argument ::= LIDENT \":\" expr | STRING \":\" expr  \n"
"\n"
"expr ::= array | object | apply | STRING | INT | \"true\" | \"false\"\n"
"array ::= \"[\" (expr \",\")* expr? \"]\"\n"
"object ::= \"{\" (field \",\")* field? \"}\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:67
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:69
msgid ""
"The package name is not configurable; it is determined by the directory "
"name of the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:71
msgid "Formatter"
msgstr "フォーマッタ"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:73
msgid ""
"The `formatter` field configures `moon fmt` for this package. Currently "
"it supports `ignore`, a list of file names that the formatter should "
"skip."
msgstr ""
"`formatter` フィールドは、このパッケージに対する `moon fmt` "
"の設定を行います。現在は、フォーマッタがスキップするファイル名の一覧である `ignore` をサポートしています。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:76
msgid ""
"This is useful for generated files or files that you intentionally keep "
"in a different format. Files produced by `pre-build` are already skipped "
"automatically, so `formatter.ignore` is mainly for additional files you "
"want to exclude."
msgstr ""
"これは、生成ファイルや、意図的に別の形式のままにしておきたいファイルに便利です。`pre-build` "
"で生成されたファイルはすでに自動でスキップされるため、`formatter.ignore` は主に追加で除外したいファイルのために使います。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md
msgid "moon.pkg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:85
msgid "formatter(ignore: [\"generated.mbt\", \"snapshot.mbt\"])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md
msgid "moon.pkg.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:92
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"formatter\": {\n"
"    \"ignore\": [\"generated.mbt\", \"snapshot.mbt\"]\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:103
msgid "Package type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:105
msgid ""
"Use one `pkgtype` declaration to specify what a package builds. For "
"example, an executable package uses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:108
msgid "pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:112
msgid ""
"The available kinds are `library`, `executable`, and `foreign_library`. "
"`library` is the default. `executable` replaces the legacy `options(\"is-"
"main\": true)`, while `foreign_library` replaces the legacy "
"`options(link: true)`. These kinds are alternatives and must not be "
"declared together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:118
msgid ""
"In a foreign-library package, `#export_name` assigns a stable symbol name"
" to a public, non-generic function in generated Wasm, JavaScript, or C "
"output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:121
msgid ""
"#export_name(\"attr_add\")\n"
"pub fn add_by_attr(n : Int32) -> Int32 {\n"
"  n + 42\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:128
msgid ""
"MoonBit currently requires export names to be valid C symbol identifiers "
"and unique within the package, regardless of the selected backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:132
msgid ""
"Known compiler issue: `#export_name` currently applies its C-symbol-"
"identifier restriction to every backend. WebAssembly export names are "
"UTF-8 strings and are not limited to C identifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:137
msgid ""
"The attribute cannot be used on generic functions or functions with "
"optional arguments. Prefer `#export_name` over backend-specific `exports`"
" link configuration for new exports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:141
msgid ""
"Export declarations are scoped to the package that produces the artifact."
" An attribute or `exports` configuration in a dependency applies when "
"that dependency is built as its own artifact, but it does not add symbols"
" to a downstream package's artifact. Define and export a wrapper in the "
"exporting package to expose dependency functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:148
msgid ""
"The native backend does not currently support exporting a "
"`foreign_library` package as a linkable library artifact, including "
"shared libraries such as a `.dll` or `.so`."
msgstr ""
"native バックエンドは現在、`foreign_library` パッケージをリンク可能なライブラリアーティファクトとしてエクスポートできません。"
"これには `.dll` や `.so` などの共有ライブラリも含まれます。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:154
msgid "is-main (deprecated)"
msgstr "is-main（非推奨）"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:156
msgid ""
"The `is-main` field is deprecated. It is still accepted for compatibility"
" with existing package files, but new and migrated `moon.pkg` files "
"should use `pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")` instead. The following legacy "
"declarations are equivalent to that `pkgtype` declaration:"
msgstr ""
"`is-main` フィールドは非推奨です。既存のパッケージファイルとの互換性のため引き続き使用できますが、新規または移行後の "
"`moon.pkg` では `pkgtype(kind: \"executable\")` を使用してください。次の旧形式の宣言は、この "
"`pkgtype` 宣言と同等です。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:161
msgid ""
"The output of the linking process depends on the backend. When this field"
" is set to `true`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:163
msgid ""
"For the Wasm and `wasm-gc` backends, a standalone WebAssembly module will"
" be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:164
msgid "For the `js` backend, a standalone JavaScript file will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:170
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  \"is-main\": true,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:179
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"is-main\": true\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:187
msgid "Importing dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:189
msgid "Import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:191
msgid ""
"The `import` field is used to specify other packages that a package "
"depends on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:193
msgid ""
"For example, the following imports `pkgA` and `pkgC`, aliasing `pkgC` to "
"`c`. User can write `@c` to access definitions from `pkgC`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:205
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"import\": [\n"
"        \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgA\",\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"path\": \"moonbit-community/language/packages/pkgC\",\n"
"            \"alias\": \"c\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"moonbitlang/core/builtin\"\n"
"    ]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:212
msgid ""
"Most core packages are not special here: if you use `@json`, `@test`, or "
"other ordinary core aliases, add the corresponding `moonbitlang/core/...`"
" package to `import` to avoid `core_package_not_imported` warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:216
msgid ""
"`prelude` is the exception. It is available by default, so the names it "
"exposes do not need an explicit package import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:219
msgid "Test import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:221
msgid ""
"The test import is used to specify other packages that the black-box test"
" package of this package depends on, with the same format as `import`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:226
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"  \"path/to/package2\" @pkg2,\n"
"} for \"test\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:234
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"test-import\": {\n"
"    \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"path\": \"path/to/package2\",\n"
"      \"alias\": \"pkg2\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:248
msgid ""
"The `test-import-all` field is used to specify whether all public "
"definitions from the package being tested should be imported (`true`) by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:250
msgid "White-box test import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:252
msgid ""
"The white-box test import is used to specify other packages that the "
"white-box test package of this package depends on, with the same format "
"as `import`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:257
msgid ""
"import {\n"
"  \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"  \"path/to/package2\" @pkg2,\n"
"} for \"wbtest\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:265
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"wbtest-import\": {\n"
"    \"path/to/package1\",\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"path\": \"path/to/package2\",\n"
"      \"alias\": \"pkg2\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:279
msgid "Maximum Concurrent Tests"
msgstr "最大同時テスト数"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:281
msgid ""
"The `max-concurrent-tests` field limits how many tests from this package "
"may run at the same time when `moon test` executes the package."
msgstr ""
"`max-concurrent-tests` フィールドは、`moon test` "
"がこのパッケージを実行するときに、このパッケージのテストを同時に実行できる数を制限します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:284
msgid ""
"This is useful when tests in the same package share ports, temporary "
"files, or other external resources that should not all run in parallel."
msgstr "同じパッケージ内のテストがポート、一時ファイル、または同時実行すべきでないその他の外部リソースを共有する場合に便利です。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:289
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  \"max-concurrent-tests\": 2,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:296
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"max-concurrent-tests\": 2\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:304
msgid "Conditional Compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:306
msgid "The smallest unit of conditional compilation is a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:308
msgid ""
"In a conditional compilation expression, three logical operators are "
"supported: `and`, `or`, and `not`, where the `or` operator can be "
"omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:310
msgid ""
"For example, `[\"or\", \"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"]` can be simplified to "
"`[\"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:312
msgid ""
"Conditions in the expression can be categorized into backends and "
"optimization levels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:314
msgid "**Backend conditions**: `\"wasm\"`, `\"wasm-gc\"`, and `\"js\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:315
msgid "**Optimization level conditions**: `\"debug\"` and `\"release\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:317
msgid "Conditional expressions support nesting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:319
msgid ""
"If a file is not listed in `\"targets\"`, it will be compiled under all "
"conditions by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:325
msgid ""
"options(\n"
"  targets: {\n"
"    \"only_js.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm_gc.mbt\": [\"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"all_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"not_js.mbt\": [\"not\", \"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_debug.mbt\": [\"debug\"],\n"
"    \"js_and_release.mbt\": [\"and\", [\"js\"], [\"release\"]],\n"
"    \"js_only_test.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"js_or_wasm.mbt\": [\"js\", \"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"wasm_release_or_js_debug.mbt\": [\"or\", [\"and\", \"wasm\", "
"\"release\"], [\"and\", \"js\", \"debug\"]]\n"
"  }\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:344
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"targets\": {\n"
"    \"only_js.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"only_wasm_gc.mbt\": [\"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"all_wasm.mbt\": [\"wasm\", \"wasm-gc\"],\n"
"    \"not_js.mbt\": [\"not\", \"js\"],\n"
"    \"only_debug.mbt\": [\"debug\"],\n"
"    \"js_and_release.mbt\": [\"and\", [\"js\"], [\"release\"]],\n"
"    \"js_only_test.mbt\": [\"js\"],\n"
"    \"js_or_wasm.mbt\": [\"js\", \"wasm\"],\n"
"    \"wasm_release_or_js_debug.mbt\": [\"or\", [\"and\", \"wasm\", "
"\"release\"], [\"and\", \"js\", \"debug\"]]\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:363
msgid "Supported Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:365
msgid ""
"The `supported_targets` field declares which backends a package is "
"intended to support. It uses a target-set expression, not an array:"
msgstr ""
"`supported_targets` "
"フィールドは、パッケージが対応する予定のバックエンドを宣言します。値には配列ではなく、ターゲット集合式を使います："

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:370
msgid "supported_targets = \"js\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:375
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"supported-targets\": \"js\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:383
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:385
msgid "`js` for a single backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:386
msgid "`+js+wasm-gc` for an explicit set of backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:387
msgid "`+all-js` for all backends except `js`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:389
msgid "Legacy array syntax is still accepted for compatibility:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:393
msgid "supported_targets = [\"js\", \"native\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:398
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"supported-targets\": [\"js\", \"native\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:406
msgid "This is package metadata, not a conditional compilation rule:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:408
msgid "use `supported_targets` to declare the package's supported backend set"
msgstr "`supported_targets` を使って、パッケージが対応するバックエンド集合を宣言する"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:409
msgid ""
"use `targets` to include or exclude individual files for different "
"backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:410
msgid ""
"use `preferred_target` in `moon.mod` to choose the default backend for "
"commands such as `moon check`, `moon run`, and `moon build`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:412
msgid ""
"When both the module and the package declare `supported_targets`, the "
"effective backend set is their intersection."
msgstr "モジュールとパッケージの両方で `supported_targets` を宣言した場合、有効なバックエンド集合は両方の宣言の積集合になります。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:415
msgid "Command behavior follows the selected backend:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:417
msgid ""
"`moon check`, `moon build`, `moon test`, and `moon bench` keep only "
"packages that support the selected backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:418
msgid "`moon run` requires the selected package to support the selected backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:419
msgid "`moon info` skips unsupported selected packages with a warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:420
msgid ""
"`moon bundle` skips package targets that do not support the selected "
"backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:422
msgid ""
"After root selection, Moon also checks reachable required dependencies. "
"If a required dependency does not support the selected backend, the "
"command fails with a normal user-facing error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:425
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:427
msgid "omitting `supported_targets` means all backends are supported"
msgstr "`supported_targets` を省略すると、すべてのバックエンドがサポート対象になる"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:428
msgid ""
"`--target all` expands to `wasm`, `wasm-gc`, `js`, and `native`, but not "
"`llvm`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:429
msgid "`llvm` is still a valid `supported_targets` value"
msgstr "`llvm` も `supported_targets` の有効な値である"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:430
msgid "legacy array syntax is deprecated, but still accepted for compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:432
msgid "A common setup is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:434
msgid "mark a native-only package with `supported_targets = \"native\"`"
msgstr "native 専用パッケージには `supported_targets = \"native\"` を設定する"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:435
msgid "set `preferred_target = \"native\"` in `moon.mod`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:436
msgid "use `targets` only when some files inside the package differ by backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:438
msgid "Native Stub Files"
msgstr "ネイティブスタブファイル"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:440
msgid ""
"The `native-stub` field lists C stub source files that should be compiled"
" with this package for native builds."
msgstr "`native-stub` フィールドは、native ビルド向けにこのパッケージと一緒にコンパイルすべき C スタブソースファイルを列挙します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:443
msgid ""
"This is commonly used together with [`extern \"C\"` declarations in the "
"FFI documentation](../../language/ffi.md), where the stub file provides "
"wrapper functions or adapter code that is easier to write in C than "
"directly in MoonBit."
msgstr ""
"これは、[FFI ドキュメントにある `extern \"C\"` 宣言](../../language/ffi.md) "
"と組み合わせて使われることが多く、その場合スタブファイルは、MoonBit で直接書くより C "
"で書く方が容易なラッパー関数やアダプタコードを提供します。"

#: ../../toolchain/moon/package.md:448
msgid "Paths are relative to the package directory."
